--
-- Regenerate with:  python tools/make-formations.py --count 88
--
-- Every point is { u, v, w } in a normalised square: `u` right, `v` up,
-- `w` depth, all in [-1, 1]. The engine maps that square onto a plane in
-- the sky, so one point set is reusable at any size, anywhere in the city,
-- facing any direction. Nothing here is in metres.
--
-- Points are spread at EQUAL ARC LENGTH along the shape, not at equal
-- parameter: equal parameter crowds drones where a curve is tight, which
-- on the heart puts two dense knots at the top of an otherwise even figure.
--
-- Every set holds exactly 88 points, because the engine refuses a formation
-- whose count is not the drone count. There is no cheap way to hide a
-- leftover drone: `visible` respawns the entity, and a light prop carries
-- its host's geometry whether the lamp is lit or not, so a parked drone is
-- a box hanging in the sky beside the picture.

